CT~~CD,~CC^~CT~ ; This is for Cache 
^XA             ; ^XA is the start type thing, and XZ the close <html> </html> type
~TA000
~JSN            ; Back feeding sequence, with parent being JS, and N is just a specific parameter type
^MMT            ; 
^MPE
~SD20
^JZY
^MFN,N
^XZ

; =====================================================================
; CH0204 ROUND LABEL - HYBRID (native Data Matrix + curved-text graphic)
; 0.443 in dia round | 600 dpi | Thermal Transfer | black-mark media
; Data Matrix data = N0423   |  curved text = CH0204-0423
; SEND RAW (not through the ZDesigner graphics driver).
; NOTE: comment lines must NOT contain a caret, or the printer reads it
; as a command. That is why commands are written plainly below (LH, BX...).
; =====================================================================

; ---- 1) Media config (mark sensing, TT, size) + SAVE --------------
^XA
^MNM,0         ; For media tracking, MN M, meansing non-cnosinous media mark sensing
^MTT           ; Thermal Transfer Media, with T being thermal transfer
^PMN           ; Decommissioning Mode, lowkey unsure what this means
^LL362         ; Label Length, LLy, x but there isn't anything there so lowkey confused
^PW400         ; Print Width PWa with a = label width in docs
^LH0,0         ; Label Home, LHx, y 0-32000 have to check the
^LS0           ; Label Shift,
^JUS           ; Configuration Update, with JUa = active config, JUS = save current settings, This is where the Nozzle Label stuff could lowkey get bad and interfear with the nozzle labels.
^XZ            ; Close Function

; ---- 2) The label ------------------------------------------------
^XA
^PW400         ; States print width
^LL362         ; Label Length
; ========== POSITION: driven by the LAYOUT KNOBS in ZPL_Script.py ===
; ^LH is left at 0,0 and the ring + Data Matrix are placed with absolute
; ^FO values computed from DESIGN_CENTER_X / DESIGN_CENTER_Y so the two
; always share ONE center. To move the whole design, change those knobs
; (NOT the numbers below -- they are regenerated every run).
; If the TOP of the ring prints cut off, lower DESIGN_CENTER_Y or re-run
; media calibration (see notes at bottom).
; ==================================================================
^LH0,0         ; LABEL HOME kept at origin; positioning is done per-field below
;
; --- curved text ring CH0204-0423 (graphic, regenerated per part/number) ---
; --- placed at FO 152,48 so its center sits on (252,150) ---
; Field origin. x,y,z This sets the upper-left corner of the field area by defining points along the x and y axis, again, from label home.
; GFa, b, c, d, data, which allows a downloaded graphic field data to a bitmap storage area. Meaning that this downloaded image / graphic is being extracted from the following text. With
; a = compression type, A = ASCII, B = Binary data, C = compressed binary, A = default
; b = Binary byte count, this should match parameter c, and if out of range values it is set to the closests one, with values 1-99999
; c = graphic field count, total number of bytes compression the graphic format, its the size of the image, not the size of the data stream.
; d = bytes per row, 1-99999, the number of bytes in a downloaded data that comprise one row of the image
; data = data, two digits per byte, LF can be inserted as needed for readability.
^FO152,48^GFA,4060,4060,20,^FS
;
; --- native Data Matrix, data = N0423, centered on (252,150) ---
^FO315,122^BXN,4,200^FDN0423^FS
; FO field location, so it chooses that to move where the data matrix will be
; then calls BXN which BX creates 2d matrix symbology, so
; BXo, h, s is all that has been used
; BXN = normal data matrix, h = dimensional height of individual element, s = quality level, which ECC 200 is recommended.
; FD defines a data string for a field, which that field is the data matrix at the slot id above
; ^FS end of the field definition which is a SCII control code also.
^XZ
